WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:25.140
"No way! Who would slash our bike tires?" Maggie cried, rushing over to her bicycle.

2
00:00:25.141 --> 00:00:29.731
"Wait," she added. "I think my tires are okay."

3
00:00:29.732 --> 00:00:32.997
"Mine too," someone else called out.

4
00:00:32.998 --> 00:00:36.646
Henry checked his bike. His tires were fine.

5
00:00:36.647 --> 00:00:41.383
"It looks like only some tires were slashed," he said.

6
00:00:41.384 --> 00:00:46.992
"Yeah. Like mine!" Cole sounded upset as he looked at his tires.

7
00:00:46.993 --> 00:00:50.058
"Who would be mean enough to do this?"

8
00:00:50.059 --> 00:00:52.549
"I don't know," Henry said.

9
00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:56.584
"But maybe The Lemonade Detectives can figure it out."

10
00:00:56.585 --> 00:01:00.861
He looked around, trying to see how everyone was reacting.

11
00:01:00.862 --> 00:01:04.062
Most of the riders looked confused or upset.

12
00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:11.673
A bunch of kids were gathered around Ms. Hernandez, asking her questions about what had happened.

13
00:01:11.674 --> 00:01:15.252
Then Henry spotted the man in the dark glasses.

14
00:01:15.253 --> 00:01:19.379
He was standing by his bike with his arms folded, looking bored.

15
00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:25.663
Maggie noticed him too. "Hey, maybe it was that guy!" she whispered.

16
00:01:25.664 --> 00:01:29.079
"I didn't see him while we were at the picnic spot.

17
00:01:29.080 --> 00:01:32.936
He could have been down here slashing tires the whole time!"

18
00:01:32.937 --> 00:01:38.059
"Maybe," Henry said. "I didn't notice him while we were up there either."

19
00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:42.494
"I bet it was those kids from Valley High School," said Cole.

20
00:01:42.495 --> 00:01:45.925
"They probably came on the ride to make trouble!"

21
00:01:45.926 --> 00:01:49.137
Henry looked around for the Valley High teens.

22
00:01:49.138 --> 00:01:53.802
He couldn't see the girl in the crowd, but he spotted the boy right away.

23
00:01:53.803 --> 00:01:57.635
He was smirking as he watched everyone check their tires.

24
00:01:57.636 --> 00:02:00.678
"His tires look okay," Cole said.

25
00:02:00.679 --> 00:02:03.347
"And we already know he doesn't like Belltown.

26
00:02:03.348 --> 00:02:05.995
Remember how he was teasing Nathan?"

27
00:02:05.996 --> 00:02:10.627
"Yeah. He should be a suspect too," Henry said.

28
00:02:10.628 --> 00:02:13.446
"Did anyone see him at the picnic area?"

29
00:02:13.447 --> 00:02:18.921
"I didn't," Maggie said. "So that proves it! He's guilty!"

30
00:02:18.922 --> 00:02:22.439
As usual, Maggie was jumping to conclusions.

31
00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:26.315
"It doesn't prove anything," Henry reminded her.

32
00:02:26.316 --> 00:02:30.678
"There were lots of people I didn't notice while we were at the picnic area.

33
00:02:30.679 --> 00:02:34.417
We should start questioning everyone and see who left."

34
00:02:34.418 --> 00:02:40.463
"I remember someone who left!" Maggie said. "That rich kid, William.

35
00:02:40.464 --> 00:02:44.445
I saw him get up and walk toward the path leading down here."

36
00:02:44.446 --> 00:02:48.166
Henry remembered seeing William leave the picnic area too.

37
00:02:48.167 --> 00:02:52.930
"Okay," he said. "But that doesn't prove anything either.

38
00:02:52.931 --> 00:02:56.605
Lots of people left to walk down to the restrooms."

39
00:02:56.606 --> 00:03:02.520
Just then Jill and Ashley rushed over. "This is terrible!" Ashley cried.

40
00:03:02.521 --> 00:03:05.885
"Someone's trying to ruin our fundraiser!"

41
00:03:05.886 --> 00:03:08.721
"You have to help us," Jill added.

42
00:03:08.722 --> 00:03:13.490
"We want to hire The Lemonade Detectives to solve this horrible crime!"

43
00:03:13.491 --> 00:03:20.579
Henry smiled. "I don't know if I'd call it a horrible crime," he said.

44
00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:24.139
"But don't worry. We're already on the case.

45
00:03:24.140 --> 00:03:27.266
To start, we want to question you two."

46
00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:30.124
"What?" Jill looked outraged.

47
00:03:30.125 --> 00:03:33.534
"You don't suspect us again, do you?"

48
00:03:33.535 --> 00:03:38.806
"No!" Henry said quickly. "You're not suspects this time."

49
00:03:38.807 --> 00:03:40.865
He knew why Jill was annoyed.

50
00:03:40.866 --> 00:03:46.632
Somehow she ended up being a suspect in a lot of The Lemonade Detectives' cases.

51
00:03:46.633 --> 00:03:49.211
Ashley had been a suspect once too.

52
00:03:49.212 --> 00:03:52.630
Henry was pretty sure that they were innocent again now.

53
00:03:52.631 --> 00:03:56.279
Why would they try to ruin a fundraiser for their own team?

54
00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:59.949
"So what do you want to ask us?" Ashley asked.

55
00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:04.028
"Do you know how many bikes got damaged?" Henry asked.

56
00:04:04.029 --> 00:04:09.782
Ashley shrugged. "We're not sure exactly," she said.

57
00:04:09.783 --> 00:04:12.538
"We'll have to check with Ms. Hernandez.

58
00:04:12.539 --> 00:04:16.482
But at least six or seven bikes have slashed tires."

59
00:04:16.483 --> 00:04:21.392
"We were just trying to figure out who left the picnic spot," Cole added.

60
00:04:21.393 --> 00:04:23.630
"Did you notice anyone slipping away?"

61
00:04:23.631 --> 00:04:28.622
"Oh." Jill looked less upset now that she realized she wasn't a suspect.

62
00:04:28.623 --> 00:04:32.292
"I don't know. I wasn't paying much attention to that."

63
00:04:32.293 --> 00:04:38.093
"Yeah," Ashley said. "I walked down to the restrooms with a couple of friends.

64
00:04:38.094 --> 00:04:41.918
The only person there when we left was your friend Nathan."

65
00:04:41.919 --> 00:04:46.777
Henry nodded, remembering that Nathan had gone to the restroom alone.

66
00:04:46.778 --> 00:04:50.450
He was sure his friend hadn't slashed those tires.

67
00:04:50.451 --> 00:04:53.823
But maybe Nathan had seen something suspicious.

68
00:04:53.824 --> 00:04:58.349
"Thanks," Henry said. "We'd better start investigating.

69
00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:00.821
What are you going to do about the ride?"

70
00:05:00.822 --> 00:05:04.961
"Good question." Cole frowned as he looked at his bike again.

71
00:05:04.962 --> 00:05:07.819
"I can't ride with a slashed tire."

72
00:05:07.820 --> 00:05:12.019
"I think Ms. Hernandez is calling Belltown Bikes."

73
00:05:12.020 --> 00:05:16.580
Ashley glanced over at the coach, who was talking on her cell phone.

74
00:05:16.581 --> 00:05:21.396
"She's going to ask them to bring new tires to replace the slashed ones."

75
00:05:21.397 --> 00:05:23.348
"Good," Henry said.

76
00:05:23.349 --> 00:05:27.738
"That should give us some time to question people before the ride continues."

77
00:05:27.739 --> 00:05:30.536
"Yeah." Jill didn't look happy.

78
00:05:30.537 --> 00:05:33.420
"But someone will have to pay for the new tires.

79
00:05:33.421 --> 00:05:41.646
So if you guys don't solve the mystery, we might not raise enough money to buy our uniforms!"
